[*] GTKWave save file -- channel 3 SRAM occupancy and everything that moves it
[*]
[*] THE FAULT: ch3 wedges with both virtual counts reading 512 on a 512-entry
[*] buffer -- alloc says EMPTY (space_free=512, 6979.14us) and drain says FULL
[*] (data_avail=512, 7023.87us), 44.7us apart. Neither wrapped, neither exceeded
[*] depth. Each is well-formed alone; together they are impossible.
[*]
[*] THREE pointer pairs feed this, groups 2a/2b/2c below:
[*]   2a u_alloc_ctrl   wr_ptr += wr_size on RESERVATION, rd_ptr += 1 on actual
[*]   2b u_drain_ctrl   wr_ptr += 1 on actual, rd_ptr += rd_size on RESERVATION
[*]   2c u_channel_fifo the real memory pointers -- GROUND TRUTH
[*]
[*] HOW TO READ IT: fifo_count (group 1) is the physical occupancy, brought out
[*] at sram_controller_unit.sv:235 and consumed by NOTHING. The drain accounting
[*] never consults it. Compare it against the virtual counts:
[*]   A) axi_wr_drain_size > fifo_count at a request -> reservations outran real
[*]      data; the virtual accounting is the bug. Confirm in 2b.
[*]   B) drain_data_available climbs to ~512 while fifo_count stays sane -> it got
[*]      there another way; 2b r_rd_ptr_bin vs r_wr_ptr_bin says which.
[*] The code comment at sram_controller_unit.sv:284-300 already describes the
[*] mechanism for (B): rd_ptr overshoots wr_ptr, the wrap-corrected count
[*] evaluates to ~DEPTH, then both pointers advance in lockstep and it is
[*] permanent. 2b shows that directly -- watch rd_ptr cross wr_ptr.
[*]
[*] WHY THE EXISTING ASSERTION PROVED NOTHING: the over-drain $error at
[*] stream_drain_ctrl.sv:176 compares rd_size against data_available -- the same
[*] REGISTERED count the write engine already compensates for (group 4:
[*] w_effective_avail = avail - w_pending_drain, a 2-cycle window matching the
[*] two flops on the path). The engine guarantees rd_size <= that number, so the
[*] check is tautological. It not firing means the engine obeyed the protocol,
[*] NOT that the reservation was physically backed.
[*]
[*] TIMELINE: 6970.58-.60us kick (all 8 accepted) | 6977.91 rd_arready drops |
[*] 6979.14 space_free[3]=512 | 7018.97 wr_wvalid drops | 7023.87
[*] drain_avail[3]=512 | 7023.93 rd_rready drops -- wedged. Markers are on the
[*] two count events; both stalled boundary signals are STREAM outputs, and the
[*] perf endpoints (LFSR gen + CRC sink, hardcoded OKAY) cannot backpressure.
[*]
